1. TTM-R3 GIFT-Eval runner (ttm/run_ttm_r3.py, ttm/src/, ttm/resources/)
   Copyright contributors to the TSFM project, Apache License 2.0 (see ttm/LICENSE-granite-tsfm).
   Source: https://github.com/ibm-granite/granite-tsfm, branch ttm-r3-release-mq2, commit e911cd1,
   notebooks/hfdemo/tinytimemixer/full_benchmarking/gift_leaderboard_ttm_r3_nc/.
   Modifications made by the authors for the paper:
     - LoRA fine-tuning through PEFT (r, alpha, dropout, target modules), with the multi-quantile head
       fully trained, and logging of the trainable parameters;
     - step-based training: at most 4,000 steps, validation, checkpointing and logging every 30 steps
       (instead of once per epoch), best checkpoint restored with early stopping;
     - sample caps lowered to 100,000 training / 10,000 validation windows, applied to the full-shot
       setting as well when -ubfs is set; seeded sampling of the validation subset;
     - configurable random seed (-seed), sequential processing of the datasets with memory release,
       detection of failed fine-tuning runs, SLURM-aware Ray initialization;
     - LoRA-aware learning-rate finder signature (tsfm_public/toolkit/lr_finder.py; not used here since
       all fine-tuning scripts set the learning rate, so the public tsfm_public at commit e911cd1 is used).
   Repository-only modifications: local imports, configurable output directory, optional dataset/horizon
   subset.

